@@@ problem c18 sort-an-array
title: Sort an Array (Quicksort)
difficulty: Medium
topics: Sorting, Divide and Conquer, Recursion
params: arr
time: O(n log n) average
space: O(log n)
bench: n=64..1048576 time=nlogn space=logn unit=n

=== description
Implement `void sort_array(int *arr, int n)`, which sorts the `n` integers of `arr` in ascending order, **in place**, in O(n log n) time. Do not call `qsort`.

Quicksort is the classic choice; make sure already-sorted input and many duplicates don't make it quadratic.

=== constraints
- `0 <= n <= 10^6`
- values fit in `int`

=== hints
- Choose the pivot at random (or median-of-three) so sorted input is not a worst case.
- A three-way partition (`< pivot`, `== pivot`, `> pivot`) handles duplicates gracefully.
- Recurse on the smaller part first and loop on the larger one to keep the stack O(log n).

=== template
/* Sort arr[0..n-1] in ascending order, in place. */
void sort_array(int *arr, int n) {
    /* your code here */
}

=== driver
extern "C" void sort_array(int *arr, int n);
LC_DRIVER {
    h.custom([](lc::Case &c) {
        auto v = c.arg<std::vector<int>>();
        c.time([&] { sort_array(v.data(), (int)v.size()); });
        c.out(v);
    });
    h.gen([](lc::Gen &g, int n) {
        int kind = g.irange(0, 3);
        auto v = g.ints(n, kind == 3 ? -3 : -1000000000, kind == 3 ? 3 : 1000000000);
        if (kind == 1) std::sort(v.begin(), v.end());
        if (kind == 2) std::sort(v.rbegin(), v.rend());
        return lc::lines(v);
    });
}

=== approach
**Quicksort with a random pivot and three-way partitioning.** Partition `arr[lo..hi]` into `< pivot`, `== pivot` and `> pivot` (Dutch national flag). The middle block is in its final place. Recurse into the **smaller** outer part and continue the loop with the larger one: that bounds the recursion depth by O(log n) even in bad cases.

A random pivot makes the expected time O(n log n) for every input order, and the three-way partition keeps arrays full of duplicates fast.

=== solution
static unsigned int seed = 2463534242u;
static unsigned int next_rand(void) {           /* xorshift PRNG */
    seed ^= seed << 13;
    seed ^= seed >> 17;
    seed ^= seed << 5;
    return seed;
}

static void swap_int(int *a, int *b) { int t = *a; *a = *b; *b = t; }

static void quicksort(int *arr, int lo, int hi) {
    while (lo < hi) {
        int pivot = arr[lo + (int)(next_rand() % (unsigned int)(hi - lo + 1))];
        /* [lo, lt) < pivot, [lt, i) == pivot, (gt, hi] > pivot */
        int lt = lo, i = lo, gt = hi;
        while (i <= gt) {
            if (arr[i] < pivot) swap_int(&arr[i++], &arr[lt++]);
            else if (arr[i] > pivot) swap_int(&arr[i], &arr[gt--]);
            else i++;
        }
        /* recurse on the smaller side, loop on the larger one */
        if (lt - lo < hi - gt) {
            quicksort(arr, lo, lt - 1);
            lo = gt + 1;
        } else {
            quicksort(arr, gt + 1, hi);
            hi = lt - 1;
        }
    }
}

void sort_array(int *arr, int n) {
    if (n > 1) quicksort(arr, 0, n - 1);
}

=== examples
[5,2,3,1]
> [1,2,3,5]

[5,1,1,2,0,0]
> [0,0,1,1,2,5]

